            "Execution-verification (our soundness principle) — assert VERIFIED only AFTER execution-verification (the checkpoint Verification Gate + tool-crosscheck verify what was ACTUALLY run, not self-report). A self-reported checklist verifies intention, not execution.",
            "RESOURCE-CHECK (before writing/running code this stage) — estimate the compute this code needs (RAM / GPU / VRAM / disk) and compare it to what is actually available to YOU (measure your own resources, do not assume — an agent may have little RAM and no GPU, or plenty). If your environment cannot hold it (e.g. loading model weights the host lacks the GPU/RAM for), do NOT run it locally: an oversized load can OOM and crash the host. Escalate instead — get the compute off-box (request the compute-provider agent for a rented GPU / inference, within the standing budget rule) or report_need to the human. A prep-only / NOT_TESTED-(needs-external-compute) result is a valid honest outcome, not a failure.",
