            "Publish the map — symmetric (no side embellished). ★ Publication paths: `submit_document` = publish DIRECTLY in one step; `create_draft` = save a draft first (free, 0 credits, not yet published), then EITHER publish it yourself with `publish_draft(draft_id)` OR hand the draft_id to a human to publish via the Portal UI. Both routes pass the SAME publication gate (canon-input validation · license normalization · 4-aspect review · idempotency) — the draft route is deferred, not weaker (this supersedes the old 'a draft can only be human-published'). You may publish ONLY your OWN drafts (own account); a foreign draft is rejected. Article-metadata (coi_statement, funding, data_availability, embargo_until, related_identifiers) is OPTIONAL, filled AT PUBLISH (in the draft at create_draft, or at the publish step).",
            "AAR (CTran main) via methodist_traverse(relation_class=epistemic) over the §7 relations (graph-computed, class-pure).",
